# Every claim filed as a single value, beside what it says would narrow it. One row per such claim
# anywhere in a document, `violates` where the answer is anything but `notApplicable`.
#
# A single value has nothing to narrow
#   The rule: a point value files narrowsWhen as notApplicable, having no range. A figure with no
#   width has nothing to tighten, so any other answer is a sentence nobody can act on: a paste from
#   a neighbouring claim, or a claim filed at the wrong width.
#
# `unmeasured` is a violation too
#   A test for a stated narrowing cannot see it. A single value answering "nobody has said what
#   would narrow this" passes such a test, but that answer assumes there is something to narrow:
#   on a single value the question is not unanswered, it does not apply, and those are different
#   facts.
#
# The stricter of the two readings
#   The roster sentence says the claim files `notApplicable`, not merely that it files no
#   condition, and every single-value claim in the corpus does. What would refute the strictness
#   is a single value with an honest reason to answer otherwise. `derived` would be the candidate,
#   and `tests/state_coverage.rs` rules it out for a narrowing, so the strict form stands.
#
# Written against `pm.claim`, not against demands
#   `narrowsWhen` is on `Claim`, and claims are everywhere. Written over the demand columns alone,
#   the rule could reach a claim's width only through the table of the thing it describes, and no
#   demand in the corpus is a single value, so it would examine nothing and the coverage table
#   would say so. Against `pm.claim` it examines every single-value claim in every document.
-- pm:Claim/pm:narrowsWhen on any pm:Claim where low = high.
SELECT r.rule, p.filing, p.layer, p.violates, p.detail
FROM      (
    :compose(checks/roster.sqlc)
) r
LEFT JOIN (
    SELECT c.filing, c.layer,
           c.narrows_absent IS DISTINCT FROM 'notApplicable' AS violates,
           format('%s claim %s: %s exactly, and it still answers %s', c.owns, c.seq, c.mode,
                  coalesce(c.narrows_kind::text, 'absent: ' || c.narrows_absent)) AS detail
    FROM (
        :compose(epistemics/point_claims.sqlc)
    ) c
) p ON true
WHERE r.slug = 'narrows_a_point_value'
